  "content": "<div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iPGG!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8a146776-b8d2-4c2e-816a-e303163b18d6_1840x1201.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><source type=\"image/webp\" /><img alt=\"\" class=\"sizing-normal\" height=\"950\" src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iPGG!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8a146776-b8d2-4c2e-816a-e303163b18d6_1840x1201.jpeg\" width=\"1456\" /><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-tqxFUX\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-tqxFUX\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">photo cred: my dad</figcaption></figure></div><h1>1.</h1><p>A few years ago, some researchers put ants and humans in a head-to-head battle of wits. The task was to maneuver an awkwardly sized object through a series of obstacles, like this:</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iDyx!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4ec5aa0d-292c-46c3-90ad-db14b7bd2ce1_2644x1394.png\" target=\"_blank\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><source type=\"image/webp\" /><img alt=\"\" class=\"sizing-normal\" height=\"768\" src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iDyx!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F4ec5aa0d-292c-46c3-90ad-db14b7bd2ce1_2644x1394.png\" width=\"1456\" /><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-tqxFUX\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-tqxFUX\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Humans and ants competed both as individuals and in groups. The humans were forbidden from communicating with one another (I guess to make the playing field more level with the ants?), and they were made to wear sunglasses and masks to prevent any nonverbal signals. The ants were allowed to do whatever they wanted, on account of them being ants. Researchers &#8220;incubated&#8221; the objects in cat food and rubbed them with tuna to make them &#8220;seem like attractive food items to the ants&#8221; (I assume humans were spared this step).</p><p>I have read the paper multiple times and I still don&#8217;t really understand why they did any of this, but <a href=\"https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2414274121\">the videos they made are really cool</a>:</p><div class=\"native-video-embed\"></div><p>I bring this up because watching those videos, I think to myself: that&#8217;s exactly what writing is. It&#8217;s maneuvering an awkwardly sized idea into someone&#8217;s head. It&#8217;s getting the thing wedged in the wrong spot and then backing up to reorient it. It&#8217;s wondering why something that looks so easy can be so hard. And occasionally, the whole thing reeks of tuna.</p><h1>2.</h1><p>Trying to write drives most people nuts, but nobody ever told me that there&#8217;s a good nuts and a bad nuts.</p><p>Bad nuts is when you&#8217;re sitting there thinking the same thing over and over again, or thinking nothing at all, just drumming your fingers on the desk and checking your email every 17 seconds, like &#8220;hmm...words...words...what <em>is </em>a word...&#8221;. This is both painful and pointless.</p><p>Good nuts is when you&#8217;re trying a million things a minute and almost all of them are failing. Like:</p><blockquote><p>Does it go like this?</p><p>No.</p><p>Does it go like <em>this</em>?</p><p>No.</p><p>Does it go like THIS?</p><p>No.</p><p>Does it go like t*h*i*s?</p><p>No.</p><p>Does it go like <em>T~H~I~S</em>?</p><p>YES</p></blockquote><p>This is also painful, but it ultimately results in something that you want to show other people. In this way, it is very similar to getting your unibrow waxed.</p>\n      <p>\n          <a href=\"https://www.experimental-history.com/p/everything-i-know-about-writing\">\n              Read more\n          </a>\n      </p>"
